<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29347" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mōab</span></b> , f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>indecl., the
				mountainous region on the eastern coast of the Dead Sea,
				extending from Zoar to the river Arnon</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Gen.
				36, 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">48, 15</span></i> and 20, etc.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mōăbītēs</span></b> ,
				ae, m., <i>an inhabitant
				of Moab, a Moabite</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1</span></i>
			Chron. 11, 46.—<i>Plur.</i>: Moabitae (=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μωαβῖται</span>), <i>the
				Moabites</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Gen. 19, 37</span></i> et
			saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mōăbītis</span></b> ,
				tĭdis, f. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μωαβῖτις</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>Moabite</i> (sc. regio), <i>the land
				of the Moabites, Moab</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Ruth,
				1, 1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Subst., a Moabitish woman</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Vulg. Ruth, 1, 22</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
